  {
   "name": "Building Decarbonization and Electrify Medford Campaign",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The committee pursued residential and building electrification initiatives, examining heat pump technology, regional coaching models, and financing options (M05#2, M07#8, M12#6). Using a grant from MassCEC, the city launched the Electrify Medford program to recruit and train energy coaches to assist residents with heat pump retrofits and energy assessments (M13#5, M17#6, M21#2). The committee also tracked decarbonization efforts across municipal properties, including school HVAC upgrades and heat pump installations (M18#3, M22#3, M26#5). Electrify Medford outreach and home electrification support continued alongside advocacy for Mass Save funding (M28#4, M31#2, M31#5, M34#2).",
